nging while the run is stuck — exactly the case where they must NOT sleep.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Make a missing budget itself an attention-raising condition, not an evaluation opt-out. Apply a default silence budget (or an execution-level fallback) so any node silent past it flips attention to needs-attention with kind \"silence_exceeded\"; reserve \"unknown\" for the first moments after start, and never let \"unknown\" persist unbounded on a running node.","severity":"critical"},{"claim":"A real failure is invisible at a glance. Event seq 11 records flaky_check outcome \"retryable_failure\", reason \"tool_exited_non_zero\", with evidence refs, and the node dropped back to queued. status reports failed: 0, queued: 1, untriagedInterruptions: [], and no attentionReason for flaky_check. The retrying/flapping node is indistinguishable from a node that is normally waiting; only a full event-tail read (a second, non-glance step) reveals it.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Surface failure history in the status summary: add counters/fields such as retryingNodes, recentFailures (node, reason, count, lastAt), and include a retry-after-failure node in attentionReasons. A node that has failed and not yet re-succeeded should not be summarized under the same bucket as a fresh queued node.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"There is no wake path for a stall. wake_arm/wake_wait ring only on content appends past the cursor; two consecutive blocking waits (60s then 120s) both returned outcome \"timeout\" while the execution was frozen mid-run. Sleeping is therefore only safe when the graph is making progress — the silent-hang case, the one the operator most needs to be woken for, produces no ring by construction.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Add a deadline/liveness ring: let wake_arm accept an attention-change or silence-deadline trigger (e.g. armOn: \"attention_change\" | \"silence_exceeded\", or a maxSilenceSeconds) so the lease rings when the log STOPS moving as well as when it moves. Distinguish the timeout reply from a \"still healthy, nothing due\" reply so the operator can tell an idle wait from a stalled run.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"status ships absolute timestamps only (lastEventAt, nodeLastEventAt, startedAt) and no elapsed/age or expected-duration fields. To notice that judge has been silent for minutes the operator must fetch wall-clock time and subtract per node — arithmetic, not a glance. Nothing in the payload states \"judge silent 4m\".","evidence":[],"remediation":"Include derived staleness in the status payload: perNode silenceSeconds, executionSilenceSeconds, and (where a budget exists) budgetRemainingSeconds, so staleness is readable without external clock math.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"attentionReasons state a cause but no operator action. \"no_declared_budget\" on node judge tells the operator why the monitor is mute; it does not tell them whether to wait, inspect, or intervene, and the MCP surface exposes no way to declare a budget on a live execution to resolve the unknown.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Attach a suggested action and a resolving affordance to each attention reason (e.g. nextAction: \"declare budget or inspect node\" plus a tool that sets/overrides a node's silence budget on a running execution), so an \"unknown\" is actionable rather than terminal.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"The glance view omits the operator's own liveness posture. status does not indicate whether any wake lease is armed; wake_status is a separate call and returned live: false before arming. An operator can read a benign-looking status, sleep, and be unaware that nothing is watching on their behalf.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Include a compact lease summary in status (armed: bool, cursor, lastConsumed) so \"is anything set to wake me?\" is answered by the same single call as \"is anything wrong?\".","severity":"low"}],"gateId":"judge-usefulness","nodeId":"judge","passed":false},"type":"gate_verdict"},"occurredAt":"2026-08-18T21:35:27.588046300Z","previousHash":"sha256:c03320bc06ca4479b19596a5980c5c63db976def3dad67981899588e5febda95","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge6bb","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"sensitivity":"internal","sequence":16,"streamId":"exec-m08-judge6bb"}],"evidenceIds":["exec-exec-m08-judge6bb-judge-a1-judgment"],"expectedNextSequence":15,"formatVersion":"1.0.0","requestDigest":"sha256:de89a94d920f28f39dcf1186b570229e1fa3825b9c960e7273f797a589b87254","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge6bb","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"streamId":"exec-m08-judge6bb"}
